<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="generated_at" content="{{ ctx.generated_at.isoformat() }}">
<title>{{ ctx.experiment_name | replace("-", " ") | title }} Experiment — A/B Analysis</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #ffffff;
    --fg: #1f2937;
    --muted: #6b7280;
    --line: #e5e7eb;
    --accent-A: {{ variant_colors["A"] }};
    --accent-B: {{ variant_colors["B"] }};
    --good: #d1fae5;
    --bad: #fee2e2;
    --warn: #fef3c7;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html, body {
    margin: 0; padding: 0;
    background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg);
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  main { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px; }
  h1 { font-size: 28px; margin: 0 0 8px 0; }
  h2 { font-size: 22px; margin: 32px 0 12px 0; padding-bottom: 6px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line); }
  h3 { font-size: 18px; margin: 20px 0 8px 0; color: var(--fg); }
  p { margin: 8px 0; }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 12px 0; font-size: 14px; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 8px 10px; text-align: right; }
  th { background: #f9fafb; text-align: left; }
  td:first-child, th:first-child { text-align: left; }
  tbody tr:nth-child(even) { background: #fafafa; }
  .verdict { font-weight: 700; padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 4px; }
  .verdict-ship { background: var(--good); color: #065f46; }
  .verdict-do_not_ship { background: var(--bad); color: #991b1b; }
  .verdict-inconclusive { background: var(--warn); color: #92400e; }
  .sig-positive { background: var(--good); }
  .sig-negative { background: var(--bad); }
  .chart { margin: 12px 0 24px 0; }
  .grid-2 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; }
  footer { margin-top: 48px; padding: 16px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
  .swatch-A { display: inline-block; width: 12px; height: 12px; background: var(--accent-A); border-radius: 2px; margin-right: 4px; vertical-align: middle; }
  .swatch-B { display: inline-block; width: 12px; height: 12px; background: var(--accent-B); border-radius: 2px; margin-right: 4px; vertical-align: middle; }
</style>
<script>{{ plotly_bundle|safe }}</script>
</head>
<body>
<main>

<h1>{{ ctx.experiment_name | replace("-", " ") | title }} Experiment — A/B Analysis</h1>
<p class="muted">
  Date range: {{ ctx.date_range[0].strftime('%Y-%m-%d') }} → {{ ctx.date_range[1].strftime('%Y-%m-%d') }}
  · <span class="swatch-A"></span>Variant A (control)
  · <span class="swatch-B"></span>Variant B (treatment)
</p>

{# ============== EXECUTIVE SUMMARY ============== #}
<section id="exec-summary">
<h2>Summary</h2>
<p><strong>Recommendation:</strong>
  {% if ctx.exec_summary.recommendation == "ship" %}
    <span class="verdict verdict-ship">SHIP</span>
  {% elif ctx.exec_summary.recommendation == "do_not_ship" %}
    <span class="verdict verdict-do_not_ship">DO NOT SHIP</span>
  {% else %}
    <span class="verdict verdict-inconclusive">INCONCLUSIVE — needs more data</span>
  {% endif %}
</p>
<p>{{ ctx.exec_summary.headline_engagement }}</p>
<p>{{ ctx.exec_summary.headline_redirect }}</p>
<p><em>{{ ctx.exec_summary.rationale }}</em></p>
</section>

{# ============== DATA OVERVIEW ============== #}
<section id="data-overview">
<h2>Data Overview</h2>
<div style="display:flex; gap:32px; flex-wrap:wrap;">
<table style="width:auto;">
  <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Rows loaded</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>ots_chat.csv</td><td>{{ "{:,}".format(ctx.chat_rows) }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>redirects.csv</td><td>{{ "{:,}".format(ctx.redirect_rows) }}</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<table style="width:auto;">
  <thead><tr><th>Variant</th><th>Distinct utids in ots_chat</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>A (control)</td><td>{{ "{:,}".format(ctx.variant_population.A) }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>B (treatment)</td><td>{{ "{:,}".format(ctx.variant_population.B) }}</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
{% if ctx.excluded_utids_count > 0 %}
<p class="muted">{{ ctx.excluded_utids_count }} utid(s) excluded due to in-file variant conflict.</p>
{% endif %}
</section>

{# ============== ENGAGEMENT ============== #}
<section id="engagement">
<h2>Engagement Analysis</h2>

{# Build lookup: dimension → INTENT metric, dimension → SUGGESTIONS metric #}
{% set _intent_map = {} %}
{% set _suggest_map = {} %}
{% for m in ctx.engagement_metrics %}
  {% if "INTENT" in m.chat_type %}{% set _ = _intent_map.update({m.dimension: m}) %}
  {% else %}{% set _ = _suggest_map.update({m.dimension: m}) %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

<table style="width:auto">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Dimension</th>
      <th>A count</th><th>B count</th>
      <th>A rate</th><th>B rate</th>
      <th>Rel. lift</th>
      <th>p-value</th>
      <th>Verdict</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for dim in ["utid", "chat_session_id", "request_id", "correlation_id"] %}
    {% set intent = _intent_map[dim] %}
    {% set blank = (dim == "chat_session_id") %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ dim }}</td>
      <td>{% if blank %}\{% else %}{{ "{:,}".format(intent.count_A) }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if blank %}\{% else %}{{ "{:,}".format(intent.count_B) }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if blank %}\{% else %}{{ intent.value_A|fmt_pct }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if blank %}\{% else %}{{ intent.value_B|fmt_pct }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if blank %}\{% else %}{{ intent.rel_lift_pct|fmt_lift }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if blank %}\{% else %}{{ intent.p_value|fmt_p }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if blank %}\{% else %}{{ intent.directional_verdict }} / {{ intent.significance_verdict.replace('_', ' ') }}{% endif %}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
<dl class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0 0; display:grid; grid-template-columns:max-content 1fr; gap:2px 12px; font-size:13px;">
  <dt><strong>Rate</strong></dt><dd>INTENT_RECOGNITION distinct count / total chat (SUGGESTIONS + INTENT) distinct count, per dimension.</dd>
  <dt><strong>p-value</strong></dt><dd>Two-proportion z-test (α = 0.05): p &lt; 0.05 indicates that the A/B difference is unlikely due to random fluctuation.</dd>
</dl>

<h3>Rounds per session (Welch's t-test)</h3>
<table style="width:auto">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Variant</th><th>Sessions</th><th>Rounds (Mean)</th><th>Rounds (Median)</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>A</td><td>{{ "{:,}".format(ctx.rounds_metric.n_sessions_A) }}</td><td>{{ ctx.rounds_metric.mean_A|fmt_num(2) }}</td><td>{{ ctx.rounds_metric.median_A|fmt_num(2) }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>B</td><td>{{ "{:,}".format(ctx.rounds_metric.n_sessions_B) }}</td><td>{{ ctx.rounds_metric.mean_B|fmt_num(2) }}</td><td>{{ ctx.rounds_metric.median_B|fmt_num(2) }}</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>Δ mean = {{ ctx.rounds_metric.abs_diff_mean|fmt_num(3) }} ·
   relative lift = {{ ctx.rounds_metric.rel_lift_mean_pct|fmt_lift }} ·
   p = {{ ctx.rounds_metric.p_value|fmt_p }} ·
   {{ ctx.rounds_metric.directional_verdict }} / {{ ctx.rounds_metric.significance_verdict.replace('_', ' ') }}</p>

<h3>Daily trend: engagement absolute (INTENT_RECOGNITION volume)</h3>
<div class="chart">{{ trend_charts["engagement_abs"]|safe }}</div>

<h3>Daily trend: engagement ratio (INTENT_RECOGNITION / SUGGESTIONS)</h3>
<div class="chart">{{ trend_charts["engagement_ratio"]|safe }}</div>
</section>

{# ============== REDIRECT ============== #}
<section id="redirect">
<h2>Redirect Analysis</h2>
<p class="muted">
  Numerator: distinct dimension values matched to a redirect via (utid, correlation_id ↔ pre_redirect_id).<br>
  p-value: two-proportion z-test (α = 0.05).
</p>

{# ---- Part 1: All chat rows ---- #}
<h3>Part 1: All chat rows (SUGGESTIONS + INTENT)</h3>
<p class="muted">Denominator: distinct dimension values across all chat rows.</p>
<table style="width:auto">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Dimension</th>
      <th>A Num</th><th>B Num</th>
      <th>A Den</th><th>B Den</th>
      <th>A Rate</th><th>B Rate</th>
      <th>Δ (pp)</th><th>Rel. lift</th>
      <th>p-value</th><th>Verdict</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for m in ctx.redirect_metrics_all %}
    {% set blank = (m.dimension == "chat_session_id") %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ m.dimension }}</td>
      <td>{% if blank %}\{% else %}{{ "{:,}".format(m.numerator_A) }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if blank %}\{% else %}{{ "{:,}".format(m.numerator_B) }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if blank %}\{% else %}{{ "{:,}".format(m.denominator_A) }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if blank %}\{% else %}{{ "{:,}".format(m.denominator_B) }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if blank %}\{% else %}{{ m.rate_A|fmt_pct }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if blank %}\{% else %}{{ m.rate_B|fmt_pct }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if blank %}\{% else %}{{ m.abs_diff|fmt_pp }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if blank %}\{% else %}{{ m.rel_lift_pct|fmt_lift }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if blank %}\{% else %}{{ m.p_value|fmt_p }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if blank %}\{% else %}{{ m.directional_verdict }} / {{ m.significance_verdict.replace('_', ' ') }}{% endif %}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="muted" style="font-size:13px;">Leave chat_session_id blank: the SUGGESTIONS row does not have a chat_session_id, and its denominator is equivalent to Part 2, so it is not displayed repeatedly.</p>

{# ---- Part 2: INTENT rows only ---- #}
<h3>Part 2: INTENT rows only</h3>
<p class="muted">Denominator: distinct dimension values among CHAT_TYPE_INTENT_RECOGNITION rows only.</p>
<table style="width:auto">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Dimension</th>
      <th>A Num</th><th>B Num</th>
      <th>A Den</th><th>B Den</th>
      <th>A Rate</th><th>B Rate</th>
      <th>Δ (pp)</th><th>Rel. lift</th>
      <th>p-value</th><th>Verdict</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for m in ctx.redirect_metrics_intent %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ m.dimension }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.numerator_A) }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.numerator_B) }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.denominator_A) }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.denominator_B) }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.rate_A|fmt_pct }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.rate_B|fmt_pct }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.abs_diff|fmt_pp }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.rel_lift_pct|fmt_lift }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.p_value|fmt_p }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.directional_verdict }} / {{ m.significance_verdict.replace('_', ' ') }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>


<h3>Daily trend: redirect absolute</h3>
<div class="chart">{{ trend_charts["redirect_abs"]|safe }}</div>

<h3>Daily trend: redirect ratio (redirect ÷ INTENT_RECOGNITION)</h3>
<div class="chart">{{ trend_charts["redirect_ratio"]|safe }}</div>
</section>

{# ============== MAP USAGE (experiment-specific, conditional) ============== #}
{% if ctx.map_section %}
<section id="map-usage">
<h2>Map Usage Analysis</h2>
<p class="muted">
  Population: users with <code>CHAT_BOX_ENTRY_LOADED</code> in actions.csv — proxy for "rendered day view with chat box"
  (A: {{ "{:,}".format(ctx.map_section.population_A) }}, B: {{ "{:,}".format(ctx.map_section.population_B) }}).
</p>

<h3>Block 1: Map Exposure Rate</h3>
<p class="muted">% of users (CHAT_BOX_ENTRY_LOADED population) who performed each map action at least once.</p>
<table style="width:auto">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th rowspan="2" style="vertical-align:middle">Metric</th>
      <th colspan="2" style="text-align:center">A (control)</th>
      <th colspan="2" style="text-align:center">B (treatment)</th>
      <th rowspan="2" style="vertical-align:middle">Rel. lift</th>
      <th rowspan="2" style="vertical-align:middle">Δ (pp)</th>
      <th rowspan="2" style="vertical-align:middle">p-value</th>
      <th rowspan="2" style="vertical-align:middle">Verdict</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>users</th><th>rate</th>
      <th>users</th><th>rate</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for m in ctx.map_section.exposure_metrics %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ m.label }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.numerator_A) }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.rate_A|fmt_pct }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.numerator_B) }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.rate_B|fmt_pct }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.rel_lift_pct|fmt_lift }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.abs_diff|fmt_pp }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.p_value|fmt_p }}</td>
      <td class="{% if m.directional_verdict == 'positive' %}sig-positive{% elif m.directional_verdict == 'negative' %}sig-negative{% endif %}">
        {{ m.directional_verdict }} / {{ m.significance_verdict.replace('_', ' ') }}
      </td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
<div class="chart">{{ map_charts["map_exposure"]|safe }}</div>



<h3>Block 2: Redirect Funnel by Map Usage</h3>
<p class="muted">
  P(redirect | user segment), per variant. "Map users" = ≥1 MAP_MOVING or MAP_HOTEL_MARKER_CLICK.
  Denominators are users within each segment; the final row shows the overall loaded-user population as a reference.
</p>
<div style="background:var(--warn);border-left:4px solid #d97706;padding:10px 14px;margin:8px 0 12px 0;font-size:14px;border-radius:0 4px 4px 0;">
  <strong>⚠ 解读警告 (Simpson's Paradox) </strong><br>
  B 组内, "地图用户"和"非地图用户"的转化率均高于 A 组, 但整体转化率几乎持平 (见最后一行) 。这并不意味着 B 对两类用户都有益。<br><br>
  真实机制: <strong>B 的 auto-open chat 将约 10 pp 的用户从高价值"地图用户"桶 (转化率 ~35%) 推入低价值"非地图用户"桶 (转化率 ~19%) </strong>。这一组成位移 (composition shift) 抵消了 B 在各子集内看似更高的转化率。<br><br>
  各子集内"B &gt; A"是事后选择偏差的结果: 能在 auto-open chat 遮挡下仍坚持使用地图的 B 组用户, 本身意愿更强, 因此转化率更高; 这不是 B 的真实优势, 而是筛选效应。应以整体 (overall) 行作为主要参考, 而非各子集。
</div>
<table style="width:auto">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th rowspan="2" style="vertical-align:middle">Segment</th>
      <th colspan="3" style="text-align:center">A (control)</th>
      <th colspan="3" style="text-align:center">B (treatment)</th>
      <th rowspan="2" style="vertical-align:middle">Rel. lift</th>
      <th rowspan="2" style="vertical-align:middle">Δ (pp)</th>
      <th rowspan="2" style="vertical-align:middle">p-value</th>
      <th rowspan="2" style="vertical-align:middle">Verdict</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>users</th><th>redirect</th><th>rate</th>
      <th>users</th><th>redirect</th><th>rate</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for m in ctx.map_section.funnel_metrics %}
    <tr{% if loop.last %} style="border-top: 2px solid var(--line); font-weight:600"{% endif %}>
      <td>{{ m.label }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.denominator_A) }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.numerator_A) }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.rate_A|fmt_pct }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.denominator_B) }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.numerator_B) }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.rate_B|fmt_pct }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.rel_lift_pct|fmt_lift }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.abs_diff|fmt_pp }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.p_value|fmt_p }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.directional_verdict }} / {{ m.significance_verdict.replace('_', ' ') }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
<div class="chart">{{ map_charts["map_funnel"]|safe }}</div>
</section>
{% endif %}

{# ============== ENTRANCE POSITION (ai-filter-entrance, conditional) ============== #}
{% if ctx.entrance_section %}
<section id="entrance-analysis">
<h2>Entrance Position Analysis</h2>
<p class="muted">
  Variant-agnostic throughout: every metric is sliced by entrance
  (<code>loaded_area</code>), not by A/B. The {{ ctx.entrance_section.entrance_names|length }} entrance loader populations
  overlap (e.g. a user who loaded <em>inline</em> may also have loaded
  <em>map</em>); each cell is a within-entrance rate.
</p>

<h3>Block 1: Per-entrance CTR &amp; redirect rate</h3>
<p class="muted">
  Descriptive ranking of the {{ ctx.entrance_section.entrance_names|length }} entrances. <br>
  CTR = clicked utids / loaded utids. <br>
  Chat users = loaded utids with <code>CHAT_TYPE_INTENT_RECOGNITION</code> in ots_chat. <br>
  Chat rate = chat users / loaded users. <br>
  Redirect rate = redirected users / clickers (or chat users).
</p>
<table style="width:auto">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Entrance</th>
      <th>Loaded users</th>
      <th>Clicked users</th>
      <th>CTR</th>
      <th>Chat users</th>
      <th>Chat rate</th>
      <th>Redirect (clickers)</th>
      <th>Redirect rate (clickers)</th>
      <th>Redirect (chat users)</th>
      <th>Redirect rate (chat users)</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for m in ctx.entrance_section.per_entrance %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ m.entrance }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.loaded_users) }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.clicked_users) }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.ctr_per_user|fmt_pct }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.chat_users) }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.chat_rate|fmt_pct }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.redirected_clickers) }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.redirect_rate_clickers|fmt_pct }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.redirected_chat_users) }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.redirect_rate_chat_users|fmt_pct }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Block 2: Native Feature Usage by Variant Group (A vs B)</h3>
<p class="muted">
  A group: utids who loaded <em>inline</em> or <em>map</em> only (not filter / search summary).<br>
  B group: utids who loaded <em>filter</em> or <em>search summary</em> only (not inline / map).<br>
  Overlap between groups is excluded as dirty data.
</p>
<table style="width:auto">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th rowspan="3" style="vertical-align:middle">Event</th>
      <th colspan="4" style="text-align:center; border-bottom:1px solid #ccc">A</th>
      <th colspan="4" style="text-align:center; border-bottom:1px solid #ccc">B</th>
      <th colspan="3" style="text-align:center; border-bottom:1px solid #ccc">All users A vs B</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th colspan="2" style="text-align:center">
        chat-loaded only<br>
        <span class="muted" style="font-weight:400">(n={{ "{:,}".format(ctx.entrance_section.ab_group_sizes["A"]) }})</span>
      </th>
      <th colspan="2" style="text-align:center">
        all users<br>
        <span class="muted" style="font-weight:400">(n={{ "{:,}".format(ctx.entrance_section.ab_group_sizes["A_all"]) }})</span>
      </th>
      <th colspan="2" style="text-align:center">
        chat-loaded only<br>
        <span class="muted" style="font-weight:400">(n={{ "{:,}".format(ctx.entrance_section.ab_group_sizes["B"]) }})</span>
      </th>
      <th colspan="2" style="text-align:center">
        all users<br>
        <span class="muted" style="font-weight:400">(n={{ "{:,}".format(ctx.entrance_section.ab_group_sizes["B_all"]) }})</span>
      </th>
      <th rowspan="2" style="vertical-align:middle">Rel. lift</th>
      <th rowspan="2" style="vertical-align:middle">p-value</th>
      <th rowspan="2" style="vertical-align:middle">Verdict</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>users</th><th>rate</th>
      <th>users</th><th>rate</th>
      <th>users</th><th>rate</th>
      <th>users</th><th>rate</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% set event_labels = {
      "DAY_VIEW_FILTERS_USED":      "FILTERS_USED",
      "DAY_VIEW_SORT_USED":         "SORT_USED",
      "MAP_MOVING_DAY_VIEW":        "MAP_MOVING",
      "MAP_HOTEL_MARKER_CLICK":     "MAP_HOTEL_CLICK",
      "DAY_VIEW_HOTEL_CARD_CLICKED":"HOTEL_CARD_CLICK"
    } %}
    {% for row in ctx.entrance_section.native_event_ab_rates %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ event_labels.get(row.event, row.event) }}</td>
      {% for g in ["A", "A_all", "B", "B_all"] %}
      {% set c = row.cells[g] %}
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(c.numerator) }}</td>
      <td>{{ c.rate|fmt_pct }}</td>
      {% endfor %}
      {% if row.all_users_ab_stats %}
      {% set s = row.all_users_ab_stats %}
      <td>{{ s.rel_lift_pct|fmt_lift }}</td>
      <td>{{ s.p_value|fmt_p }}</td>
      <td>{{ s.directional_verdict }} / {{ s.significance_verdict.replace('_', ' ') }}</td>
      {% else %}
      <td colspan="3" style="text-align:center">—</td>
      {% endif %}
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Block 3: Native Feature Usage by Entrance</h3>
<p class="muted">
  For each entrance, % of its loaded utids who fired the native action at
  least once. Compares {{ ctx.entrance_section.entrance_names|length }} entrances side-by-side; per-column denominator
  (loader-set size) shown in the header.
</p>
<table style="width:auto">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th rowspan="2" style="vertical-align:middle">Event</th>
      {% for e in ctx.entrance_section.entrance_names %}
      <th colspan="2" style="text-align:center">
        {{ e }}<br>
        <span class="muted" style="font-weight:400">(loaded={{ "{:,}".format(ctx.entrance_section.entrance_loaders[e]) }})</span>
      </th>
      {% endfor %}
    </tr>
    <tr>
      {% for e in ctx.entrance_section.entrance_names %}
      <th>users</th><th>rate</th>
      {% endfor %}
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% set event_labels = {
      "DAY_VIEW_FILTERS_USED":      "FILTERS_USED",
      "DAY_VIEW_SORT_USED":         "SORT_USED",
      "MAP_MOVING_DAY_VIEW":        "MAP_MOVING",
      "MAP_HOTEL_MARKER_CLICK":     "MAP_HOTEL_CLICK",
      "DAY_VIEW_HOTEL_CARD_CLICKED":"HOTEL_CARD_CLICK"
    } %}
    {% for row in ctx.entrance_section.native_event_rates %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ event_labels.get(row.event, row.event) }}</td>
      {% for e in ctx.entrance_section.entrance_names %}
      {% set c = row.cells[e] %}
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(c.numerator) }}</td>
      <td>{{ c.rate|fmt_pct }}</td>
      {% endfor %}
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Block 4: With vs Without Each Entrance (Active Users Only)</h3>
<p class="muted">
  Population restricted to <strong>active utids</strong> — those who
  triggered at least one native event (FILTERS_USED, SORT_USED, MAP_*,
  HOTEL_CARD_CLICKED). This filters out passively-loaded users (e.g. B-group
  users whose filter sidebar auto-loaded but who never interacted), so the
  loaded-vs-not-loaded comparison reflects entrance position rather than
  exposure-mechanism asymmetry.
  <br><br>
  For each entrance, compare the relevant native-event rates among active
  utids who <em>loaded that entrance</em> vs active utids who <em>did not
  load it</em> (but did load some other entrance — i.e. saw the chat-box
  elsewhere). Δ&nbsp;=&nbsp;loaded&nbsp;rate&nbsp;−&nbsp;not-loaded&nbsp;rate.
</p>

{% for tbl in ctx.entrance_section.impact_tables %}
<h4 style="margin:14px 0 4px 0">{{ tbl.entrance }}</h4>
<table style="width:auto">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th rowspan="2" style="vertical-align:middle">Event</th>
      <th colspan="4" style="text-align:center">
        loaded {{ tbl.entrance }}<br>
        <span class="muted" style="font-weight:400">(n={{ "{:,}".format(tbl.loaded_users) }})</span>
      </th>
      <th colspan="4" style="text-align:center">
        not loaded {{ tbl.entrance }}<br>
        <span class="muted" style="font-weight:400">(n={{ "{:,}".format(tbl.not_loaded_users) }})</span>
      </th>
      <th colspan="2" style="text-align:center">Δ (pp)</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>users</th><th>rate</th><th>redirect</th><th>redirect rate</th>
      <th>users</th><th>rate</th><th>redirect</th><th>redirect rate</th>
      <th>event rate</th><th>redirect rate</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% set event_labels = {
      "DAY_VIEW_FILTERS_USED":      "FILTERS_USED",
      "DAY_VIEW_SORT_USED":         "SORT_USED",
      "MAP_MOVING_DAY_VIEW":        "MAP_MOVING",
      "MAP_HOTEL_MARKER_CLICK":     "MAP_HOTEL_CLICK",
      "DAY_VIEW_HOTEL_CARD_CLICKED":"HOTEL_CARD_CLICK"
    } %}
    {% for r in tbl.rows %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ event_labels.get(r.event, r.event) }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(r.loaded_event_users) }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.loaded_rate|fmt_pct }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(r.loaded_redirect_count) }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.loaded_redirect_rate|fmt_pct }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(r.not_loaded_event_users) }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.not_loaded_rate|fmt_pct }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(r.not_loaded_redirect_count) }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.not_loaded_redirect_rate|fmt_pct }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.abs_diff|fmt_pp }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.redirect_rate_diff|fmt_pp }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{% endfor %}
</section>
{% endif %}

{# ============== APPENDIX ============== #}
<section id="appendix">
<h2>Appendix</h2>

<h3>Methodology</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Engagement rate:</strong> per-dimension distinct INTENT count / per-dimension distinct count across all chat (SUGGESTIONS + INTENT). E.g. for the request_id dimension, the rate is the share of all chat request_ids that triggered an INTENT_RECOGNITION row.</li>
  <li><strong>Engagement ratio (trend chart 2):</strong> at the utid panel — distinct INTENT utids / distinct SUGGESTIONS utids per (dt, variant). At the chat_session_id panel, since SUGGESTIONS rows have empty session_id, the denominator is the SUGGESTIONS row count per (dt, variant) — interpretable as "INTENT sessions started per suggestion render".</li>
  <li><strong>Redirect attribution:</strong> a chat row is "redirected" iff its correlation_id appears in redirects.pre_redirect_id. Suggestions are excluded.</li>
  <li><strong>Statistical tests:</strong> two-proportion z-test for rate metrics; Welch's t-test for the rounds mean. α = {{ ctx.alpha }}. Two-sided.</li>
  <li><strong>Significance verdict:</strong> "significant" iff p &lt; {{ ctx.alpha }}.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Multiple comparisons</h3>
<p>
  This report runs <strong>{{ ctx.total_tests }}</strong> two-sided tests in total at α = {{ ctx.alpha }}.
  At this multiplicity, the expected number of false positives under the null hypothesis is approximately
  <strong>{{ "%.2f"|format(ctx.expected_false_positives) }}</strong>. No multiple-comparisons correction
  (Bonferroni / Benjamini-Hochberg) is applied. Treat borderline-significant findings
  with this in mind.
</p>

<h3>Excluded data</h3>
<p>
  {% if ctx.excluded_utids_count == 0 %}
    No utids excluded.
  {% else %}
    {{ ctx.excluded_utids_count }} utid(s) excluded due to in-file variant conflict in ots_chat.csv.
  {% endif %}
  Cross-file variant validation (against actions.csv) is intentionally NOT performed in this analysis
  (per Clarifications session 2026-05-21).
</p>

<h3>Per-day per-variant row counts</h3>
<p class="muted">Sanity-check: for any day where one variant's row count is much smaller than the other, treat the daily-trend points with caution.</p>
{# We could render a small daily counts table here in a future iteration. #}

</section>

<footer>
  Generated {{ ctx.generated_at.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S UTC') }}
  · Source: ots_chat.csv + redirects.csv
  · Plotly bundle inlined for offline viewing
</footer>

</main>
</body>
